<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tama people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tama are a people of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, living mainly in the hills around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guereda">Guéréda</a>. They speak Tama, one of the Taman languages of the Eastern Sudanic family, and are mostly farmers and herders. By the 17th century they had formed the sultanate of Dar Tama, which was often subject to the stronger neighbouring sultanates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a> and Darfur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tama-people.jpg" alt="Tama people" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Idaltu; derivative work by Moataz Egbaria · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Darfur_2011-ar.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
